= Organized Capitalism & State Regulation

Modern capitalism in Germany has changed. Small competing businesses have been replaced by large banks, industrial cartels, and price-fixing syndicates.

As Rudolf Hilferding noted at the Kiel Congress, this means the old market system is mostly gone. Big business has already proven that large-scale planning is possible. Our goal now is not to print money recklessly, but to use the power of the state to protect workers and regulate private monopolies.

